{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Whatever has a blemish in it you shall not offer, for it will not be accepted for you.</b> As in <b>הֲיִרְצְךָ אוֹ הֲיִשָּׂא פָנֶיךָ</b> (Malachi 1:8). And after He warned regarding the burnt offering, which is קָדְשֵׁי קֳדָשִׁים, that it be male and without blemish, and clarified that this is required only for cattle and sheep, as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated: תְּמוּת וּזְכָרוּת בִּבְהֵמָה וְאֵין תְּמוּת וּזְכָרוּת בְּעוֹפוֹת — He said [this verse]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase וְאָמַר at the end (literally 'He said') appears to introduce this verse as the conclusion of the preceding warning; translated hyper-literally as 'He said [this verse].'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:20.040402273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}